"[
  {
    "stop": "files",
    "title": "Two brokers, one history",
    "intro": "A tour of the demo: made-up trades at real Banka Slovenije rates. A few cases are not in it, such as a dividend payer's details to fill in.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "trading212-2023-2026.csv",
        "mono": true,
        "body": "Trading 212, from 2 May 2023. A sale is matched with the purchases before it, so an export reaches back to the oldest of them."
      },
      {
        "lead": "ibkr-flex-2019-2026.xml",
        "mono": true,
        "body": "Interactive Brokers, from 14 Aug 2019. All files are read together, in this tab, and never uploaded. Shares bought at one broker and sold at another are matched across both."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "details",
    "title": "Details for the file header",
    "intro": "FURS needs a few details in the header of each XML file. In the demo they are optional: its files are written for a made-up taxpayer.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "Tax number (davčna številka)",
        "body": "The 8 digits FURS knows a taxpayer by. With the name and address, it goes into each file's header only; no figure depends on it. A real return needs it."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "summary",
    "title": "Estimates, split by tax rate",
    "intro": "The overview starts with what both returns add up to: the tax to pay, as an estimate.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "Estimate",
        "body": "TaxReporter prepares the return and estimates the tax. eDavki calculates the final tax, and the FURS assessment is what counts."
      },
      {
        "lead": "Net taxable gain €8,134.33",
        "body": "Gains after normed costs (1% of the purchase value and 1% of the sale value, never more than the gain), with this year's losses set against them: -€427.50."
      },
      {
        "lead": "Net taxable gain by tax rate",
        "body": "The longer shares were held, the lower the rate on their gain. Here €2,863.48\\u00a0×\\u00a025% + €5,270.85\\u00a0×\\u00a020% = €1,770.04."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "saleRate",
    "title": "A sale, its rate and its source",
    "intro": "The inventory list (popisni list) of Apple Inc.: the rows Doh-KDVP will hold for it, one for each purchase and sale.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "Adjusted for the 4:1 split of 31 Aug 2020",
        "body": "This purchase is shown in shares after the split: quantity and price restated by its 4:1 ratio. The purchase date stays, and with it the holding period."
      },
      {
        "lead": "1 EUR = 1.1547 USD",
        "body": "From Banka Slovenije's list of 12 Mar 2026, the trade date. The list quotes USD per euro, so the price is divided: USD\\u00a0214.87\\u00a0÷\\u00a01.1547 = 186.08296527, rounded to 8 decimal places."
      },
      {
        "lead": "ibkr-flex-2019-2026.xml, row 208",
        "mono": true,
        "body": "Every row names the file and the line it came from, so each figure can be checked against the broker's own export."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "holding",
    "title": "Two lots, two tax rates",
    "intro": "The 45 shares sold were matched with the purchases before the sale, oldest first. Each matched lot keeps its own holding period.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "20%",
        "body": "Held 6 years, since 14 Aug 2019. Gains are taxed at 25% under 5 completed years of holding, 20% after 5, 15% after 10, and 0% after 15."
      },
      {
        "lead": "25%",
        "body": "First in, first out: the 40 shares bought on 14 Aug 2019 went first, then 5 of the 15 bought on 3 Mar 2022. Each part keeps its own holding period."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "fifoBrokers",
    "title": "First in, first out, across brokers",
    "intro": "NVIDIA Corp. shares were bought at Trading 212 and Interactive Brokers, then sold at Interactive Brokers. Lots are matched by ISIN, whichever broker holds them.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "Trading 212",
        "body": "The oldest purchase (20, 2 May 2023) is in the Trading 212 file. It is matched first, though the sale was at Interactive Brokers."
      },
      {
        "lead": "25",
        "body": "Sold on 11 Feb 2026: the 20 from Trading 212 first, then 5 of the 15 bought at Interactive Brokers on 5 Aug 2024."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "slices",
    "title": "Small buys, oldest first",
    "intro": "Regular small buys at Trading 212, in fractions of a share and in euros, so no exchange rate applies. Then one sale of 5.2.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "15 Jan 2024",
        "body": "The oldest buys are sold first, in order: 1.3871 + 1.3304 + 1.2551 + 1.2274 = 5.2."
      },
      {
        "lead": "1.2274",
        "body": "Only 1.2274 of the 1.2287 bought on 15 Oct 2024 was needed. The rest stays held, with its own purchase date and cost."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "loss",
    "title": "A loss that counts",
    "intro": "Sold at a loss. A loss reduces the year's gains, unless the 30-day rule sets it aside.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "ASML",
        "body": "Bought on 21 Jul 2025, sold on 4 Aug 2026. A loss is set aside, in the part replaced, when the same security was bought in the 30 days before or after the sale. These files show no such purchase, so the whole loss counts."
      },
      {
        "lead": "-€427.50",
        "body": "Proceeds €3,846.90 less cost €4,274.40. A loss gets no normed costs; it is set against the year's gains."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "holiday",
    "title": "A holiday, and the list before it",
    "intro": "Doh-Div lists every dividend on its own row, converted at the rate of the day it was paid.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "€14.23",
        "body": "USD\\u00a016.65\\u00a0÷\\u00a01.1702 = €14.23: the gross in euros, rounded to the cent."
      },
      {
        "lead": "1 EUR = 1.1702 USD",
        "body": "Paid on 1 May 2026, a TARGET holiday: the euro payment system is closed and Banka Slovenije publishes no list. As for a weekend, TaxReporter uses the last list before it: 30 Apr 2026."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "treaty",
    "title": "A credit capped by the treaty",
    "intro": "Tax withheld abroad is credited against the Slovenian tax on a dividend, up to the rate in the tax treaty with that country.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "€32.49",
        "body": "Withheld in Germany on the €123.20 gross paid by Allianz SE."
      },
      {
        "lead": "€18.48",
        "body": "The treaty with Germany allows 15%: €123.20\\u00a0×\\u00a015% = €18.48. The rest of the €32.49 withheld does not reduce the Slovenian tax."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "notes",
    "title": "What the notes mean",
    "intro": "Notes say what TaxReporter found in the files and how the rules applied. None in this demo stops a return.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "Nothing blocks the download.",
        "body": "Notes come in three kinds. “Fix before you download” holds its return back until it is fixed, “Check these” is worth reading, and “For your information” needs nothing."
      },
      {
        "lead": "Trading 212: interest rows (6) are not on these returns.",
        "body": "Rows that are not on these returns are named here rather than left out without a word, so nothing in a file goes missing unnoticed."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "stop": "download",
    "title": "Download, then you submit",
    "intro": "Last stop. The demo's files are written exactly like yours, but for a made-up taxpayer: never import them into eDavki.",
    "notes": [
      {
        "lead": "Doh-KDVP",
        "body": "The return for gains on securities: one inventory list (popisni list) for each security sold. Doh-Div, beside it, lists each dividend payment on a row of its own."
      },
      {
        "lead": "Doh_KDVP_2026.xml",
        "mono": true,
        "body": "Written on this device and saved there; nothing is uploaded. In eDavki, a file like this is imported under Dokumenti, then Uvoz."
      },
      {
        "lead": "Download Doh-KDVP",
        "body": "After the import, eDavki shows the form for you to compare with these results and submit yourself. TaxReporter never files, and eDavki calculates the final tax."
      }
    ]
  }
]"
